A||N||1||turbo86se||I'm ok everyone!!||||6||
Z||000000||turbo86se||07-07-2001||11:06 AM||||<BR>Whew! Last night got a little interesting! I was out crusing in my '88 coupe, V6 purring behind me, T-Tops off, looking for the plum coupe with a black spoiler I spotted by the beach with NC plates. I couldn't find it, so I came home. As soon as I came home, my roommate and her boyfriend were right behind me, telling me of a tornado that just formed and touched down a few miles north of my house in Myrtle Beach. At this time the sky got real dark and the wind picked up. I had just had a dream about my Fiero getting picked up and totalled, so this was not good. <BR>We were lucky, the two twisters stayed away from my home in Murrells Inlet, one sat stationary for 15 minutes in MB, ripping a hotel roof off, and throwing debris everywhere. The other tornado touched down by my college, pulling huge trees from the ground, and ripping others to shreds. I've never seen anything like it. Chris Pond emailed me to see if I was alright, and I told him about a Jeep that was in the middle of a field, I'm sure it was picked up and tossed a few times!<P>From the newspaper, it says two weather patterns off coast collided to form tornadoes, causing $8 million dollars overall Myrtle Beach damage, including $6.5 million structual damage, $1 million damage to vehicles (I saw countless cars without any windows), and between $300,000 and $500,000 damage to signs. We drove by my school, where one tornado touched down, traffic lights were bent, street signs were gone, and one that says Horry Georgetown Tech College was wrapped around the base of the street light.<BR>Anyways, just wanted everyone to know I'm alright, and so are the Fieros!||||reg||6
Z||000001||Urchin||07-07-2001||11:31 AM||||Good to hear that you and your car survived.<BR>Don't have to worry about tornados to often up here....luckily.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lowered_blackgtsig2a_2.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
